adjudication.rationale:
In `_hydrateEmbedded` the new plural-handling branch (`/(.+)_id(s?)$/`) always executes `delete obj[k]` after mapping the `*_ids` array into hydrated records: 

```js
const hydrated = obj[k].map(...);
obj[self.pluralize(subType)] = hydrated || [];
delete obj[k];
```

In contrast, the singular `*_id` branch only deletes the original key when `_lookupSubType` returns a truthy hydrated object. This means when plural hydration can’t actually resolve IDs (e.g., `_lookupSubType` returns `null/undefined` for some/all IDs because the embedded records aren’t present in `root`), the code will still remove the original `*_ids` list and replace it with an array containing `undefined` entries, losing the original IDs. That is a real, verifiable behavioral divergence introduced by the diff and can break consumers that rely on the IDs when hydration fails.
